            {
                "entry_id": "b394e686-db2f-3404-8828-bd95e2c57a33",
                "word": "Microsoft",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "05010fde-1eea-478a-aa2b-febe00b84267",
                        "entry_id": "b394e686-db2f-3404-8828-bd95e2c57a33",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Microsofts"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8173826-a738-3d17-b1aa-2eed2e55a17e",
                        "entry_id": "b394e686-db2f-3404-8828-bd95e2c57a33",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A company whose products are widespread."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31ed5463-fd16-4179-a2eb-a8dc98766601",
                                "sense_id": "a8173826-a738-3d17-b1aa-2eed2e55a17e",
                                "text": "After its phenomenal stock offering two weeks ago, Netscape Communications Corp. is well on its way to becoming the Microsoft of the Internet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44a24a6a-ab39-4895-8760-fb5ce431752d",
                                "sense_id": "a8173826-a738-3d17-b1aa-2eed2e55a17e",
                                "text": "Similarly, said Fraley, farmers were going to demand Bt cotton or Roundup-resistant soybean plants no matter where they went shopping for seeds. Monsanto would be the Microsoft of agriculture."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "330f83a7-8d1d-445f-957e-e7bd6160362f",
                                "sense_id": "a8173826-a738-3d17-b1aa-2eed2e55a17e",
                                "text": "The company wanted to turn Celera into the Microsoft of the gene-hunting world, selling its version of the human genome to private or public gene hunters through a proprietary computer program."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d31af269-1122-49fe-9367-53e8f2f2ec35",
                                "sense_id": "a8173826-a738-3d17-b1aa-2eed2e55a17e",
                                "text": "Shepherding is more or less gone (though there’s an interesting move back toward discipleship in today’s church especially among those influenced by Rick Warren’s blockbuster book The Purpose-Driven Life), but Integrity remains as sort of the Microsoft of worship music."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
